---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About the demonstrations | David Blumenau" description="How the portfolio’s product recordings, interactive illustrations and source history were prepared.">
  <main id="main" class="wrap demo-notes">
    <header id="top"><a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to the work</a><p class="eyebrow">About the material</p><h1>Real products.<br /><em>Room to explore.</em></h1><p>The portfolio combines recorded product workflows with small, self-contained demonstrations. Each serves a different purpose.</p></header>
    <div class="demo-notes-body">
      <section><h2>What the recordings show</h2><p>Product screenshots and videos were captured in October 2026. They show working interfaces, with captions describing the actions. Personal information is hidden where necessary; gallery images are selected safe-for-work artwork. Edited recordings disclose cuts or shortened pauses.</p><p>The native Apple client runs in an iPhone simulator. Pencil Page uses synthetic handwriting with actual model feedback. Conference Notes uses an isolated copy of the real application, fictional attendees and an actual analysis. Its recording reviews that analysis after it completed.</p><a href="/media/media-provenance.json">Read the media provenance records ↗</a></section>
      <section><h2>What you can try here</h2><p>Forge World is an illustrated map of the projects. Its screens use real captures; its buildings, paths and movement are a designed way to explore the work.</p><p>The Memory Lab uses a reviewed technical sample from the knowledge graph. Its controls change that local sample. Source excerpts preserve the supporting wording, including historical names. The workbench diagrams explain configuration and workflow relationships.</p><p>These interactive examples run within the portfolio. They do not connect to private records or operate the underlying services.</p></section>
      <section><h2>What the history establishes</h2><p>The release explorer connects selected decisions with repository tags and source commits. Tags establish checkpoints in the code’s history. A dated capability or historical session does not, by itself, establish what is enabled in production today.</p><p>Case studies separate the source history from the workflow demonstrated in their recordings. Evidence drawers preserve useful detail without putting every technical qualification in the main story.</p><a href="/releases/">Explore the source history ↗</a></section>
      <section><h2>Files you can take away</h2><p>The Kitforge sample is an actual exported MP4. The conference PowerPoint was generated by the application and retains editable objects. Its companion PDF is rendered from that file. Fictional notes remain clearly labelled, and personal template-author metadata has been removed.</p><a href="/sample-files/sample-provenance.json">Read the sample-file provenance ↗</a></section>
      <section><h2>A few well-made building blocks</h2><p>This site uses Astro, Three.js, DM Sans and Fraunces. Fonts are served with the site. Distributed library and font notices are available below.</p><div class="demo-license-links"><a href="/licenses/three.txt">Three.js license</a><a href="/licenses/dm-sans.txt">DM Sans license</a><a href="/licenses/fraunces.txt">Fraunces license</a></div></section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .demo-notes{padding-block:40px 85px;max-width:1080px}
  header .eyebrow{color:var(--rust);margin:42px 0 20px}
  h1{font-size:clamp(3.3rem,6vw,5.7rem)}
  header>p:last-child{font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);max-width:650px;margin-top:26px}
  .demo-notes-body{margin-top:55px}
  section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.55fr;gap:14px 65px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-block:30px}
  section h2{font-size:1.85rem;grid-row:1/6;max-width:300px}
  section p,section>a,section>div{grid-column:2;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}
  section>a{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--ink);width:fit-content;padding-block:7px}
  .demo-license-links{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .demo-license-links a{font-size:.8rem}
  @media(max-width:700px){section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}section h2{grid-row:auto;max-width:none}section p,section>a,section>div{grid-column:1}}
</style>
